Figure 10 from the PDF illustrates the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 and antigen 24 hours following intramuscular injection. The top row shows Nano-11 (red) co-formulated with ovalbumin (green) accumulating within Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells at the injection site, with visible colocalization. Arrows highlight cells containing intracellular Nano-11. This indicates that Nano-11 effectively delivers adsorbed antigens to key immune cells and induces cellular infiltration, supporting its role as an adjuvant that enhances antigen uptake and presentation in vivo, a critical step for initiating an adaptive immune response.